<title>ITALY: Italy autumn durum wheat sowings seen up 1.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Italy autumn durum wheat sowings seen up 1.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's autumn durum wheat sowings in the 1996/97 crop season were seen rising 1.5 percent to some 1.70 million hectares, the Italian institute for agriculture studies (Ismea) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Ismea forecast autumn soft wheat sowings 6.7 percent down at 799,700 hectares.</p>
<p>&quot;This fall reflects the bad weather which prevented farmers from sowing in that period of the year and an increase in interest in maize and oilseeds,&quot; an Ismea spokeswoman said. --Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
</text>
